    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacco</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ātum, 1,
				v. a.
			saccus, <i>to strain through a bag</i>,
				<i>to strain</i>, <i>filter.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saccata aqua (opp. turbida),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 86, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 7, 17, § 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29, 2, 10, §
			35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">33, 6, 34,
				§ 104 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caecuba,</span>”
				<i>to filter</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 40, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of urine: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saccatus umor corporis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 1028</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 6, 77</span></i>.</div>
